 ### How do the circle's resources come back?
 
-On their own, by the book (p. 41). A new circle starts with 1 plus its members in each of Stitch, Refresh and Train (since 2026-10-13 also when its desk was first opened after members were approved: it used to start at 1 each until the seal). Spent resources do not come back after an assignment: when the circle advances on a full Illumination track, each refills to 1 plus the members. There is no Refill button (Robert's issue #66.4, 2026-10-13). A circle with Resource Management earns one back at each milestone (3, 6 and 9): the milestone's log line says so, the Lightkeeper's circle page, right under Add Illumination (and on a wide desk the charter abstract), asks "Resource Management: earn back one" with Stitch, Refresh and Train, and one press applies the circle's choice and logs it ("Resource Management: The Moths earns back a Stitch (2 of 4)."). A full resource cannot be picked; with every resource full when the milestone passes there is nothing to earn back, and the log says that instead. Several milestones passed at once wait as several only while that many points are missing: with one point missing a tally passing 3 and 6 earns one, and the second milestone's line says there is nothing more to earn back. A waiting earn-back never outlasts the points it is for: a correction, a spend given back or a member leaving that fills them takes it away, so none is banked for a later spend. Taking the track back past a milestone (a point added by mistake) takes its earn-back away, and the advance's refill clears any still waiting. The players' circle page says when one waits. The Lightkeeper's squares on each resource stay for corrections, and each press writes a log line ("The Lightkeeper set the circle's Train to 3 (was 2).").
+On their own, by the book (p. 41). A new circle starts with 1 plus its members in each of Stitch, Refresh and Train (since 2026-10-13 also when its desk was first opened after members were approved: it used to start at 1 each until the seal). Spent resources do not come back after an assignment: when the circle advances on a full Illumination track, each refills to 1 plus the members. There is no Refill button (Robert's issue #66.4, 2026-10-13). A circle with Resource Management earns one back at each milestone (3, 6 and 9): the change's one Resource Management log line names the milestone and says so (a circle without it logs no milestone line), the Lightkeeper's circle page, right under Add Illumination (and on a wide desk the charter abstract), asks "Resource Management: earn back one" with Stitch, Refresh and Train, and one press applies the circle's choice and logs it ("Resource Management: The Moths earns back a Stitch (2 of 4)."). A full resource cannot be picked; with every resource full when the milestone passes there is nothing to earn back, and the log says that instead. Several milestones passed at once wait as several only while that many points are missing: with one point missing a tally passing 3 and 6 earns one, and the second milestone's line says there is nothing more to earn back. A waiting earn-back never outlasts the points it is for: a correction, a spend given back or a member leaving that fills them takes it away, so none is banked for a later spend. Taking the track back past a milestone (a point added by mistake) takes its earn-back away while one waits (an applied one stays counted, and the milestone is not counted again on the way up), and the advance's refill clears any still waiting. The players' circle page says when one waits. The Lightkeeper's squares on each resource stay for corrections, and each press writes a log line ("The Lightkeeper set the circle's Train to 3 (was 2).").
 
